nd minimal.\n\nActually, you know, let me reconsider once more whether `from typesystem.fields import Reference` is the primary bet. The get_info output for Reference showed `from typesystem.fields import Field` \u2014 if that's the actual module header of the file defining Reference, then Reference is NOT in fields.py, and `from typesystem.fields import Reference` would fail. The header for SchemaDefinitions showed `from collections.abc import MutableMapping` \u2014 if that's the actual header of schemas.py, it contradicts the snippet showing `from typesystem.fields import Array, Field, Object`. So the headers are NOT actual module headers \u2014 they're synthesized minimal context. \n\nGiven synthesized context, Reference's location is unknown. The defensive import handles both cases. But which order? If I try schemas first and it fails, fall back to fields. If schemas has it (either defined or imported), we get the exact class used by set_definitions. \n\nHmm wait, actually there's another subtlety: what if `typesystem.schemas` doesn't exist as importable... no, the snippet is from typesystem/schemas.py, it exists.\n\nAlso `SchemaDefinitions` \u2014 the snippet's signature annotates `definitions: SchemaDefinitions`, so SchemaDefinitions is in schemas.py namespace. `from typesystem.schemas import SchemaDefinitions` works.\n\nNow, the tests. Let me design them:\n\n```python\nimport pytest\n\nfrom typesystem.fields import Array, Field, Object\nfrom typesystem.schemas import SchemaDefinitions, set_definitions\n\ntry:\n    from typesystem.schemas import Reference\nexcept ImportError:\n    from typesystem.fields import Reference\n\n\ndef test_set_definitions_on_reference():\n    \"\"\"Lines 37-38: Reference with definitions=None gets definitions set.\"\"\"\n    definitions = SchemaDefinitions()\n    field = Reference(to=\"Pet\")\n    assert field.definitions is None\n    set_definitions(field, definitions)\n    assert field.definitions is definitions\n\n\ndef test_set_definitions_on_reference_with_existing_definitions():\n    \"\"\"Branch of line 37: Reference with definitions already set is left alone.\"\"\"\n    existing = SchemaDefinitions()\n    definitions = SchemaDefinitions()\n    field = Reference(to=\"Pet\", definitions=existing)\n    set_definitions(field, definitions)\n    assert field.definitions is existing\n\n\ndef test_set_definitions_on_array_without_items():\n    \"\"\"Branch of line 40: Array with items=None is a no-op.\"\"\"\n    definitions = SchemaDefinitions()\n    field = Array()\n    assert field.items is None\n    set_definitions(field, definitions)\n    assert field.items is None\n\n\ndef test_set_definitions_on_array_with_list_items():\n    \"\"\"Lines 41-43: Array with a list of items recurses into each child.\"\"\"\n    definitions = SchemaDefinitions()\n    children = [Reference(to=\"A\"), Reference(to=\"B\"), Field()]\n    field = Array(items=children)\n    set_definitions(field, definitions)\n    assert children[0].definitions is definitions\n    assert children[1].definitions is definitions\n    assert children[2].definitions is None  # plain Field untouched\n\n\ndef test_set_definitions_on_array_with_single_item():\n    \"\"\"Line 45: Array with a single Field item recurses into it.\"\"\"\n    definitions = SchemaDefinitions()\n    child = Reference(to=\"A\")\n    field = Array(items=child)\n    set_definitions(field, definitions)\n    assert child.definitions is definitions\n\n\ndef test_set_definitions_on_object_properties():\n    \"\"\"Lines 46-48: Object recurses into each property.\"\"\"\n    definitions = SchemaDefinitions()\n    child_a = Reference(to=\"A\")\n    child_b = Reference(to=\"B\")\n    field = Object(properties={\"a\": child_a, \"b\": child_b})\n    set_definitions(field, definitions)\n    assert child_a.definitions is definitions\n    assert child_b.definitions is definitions\n\n\ndef test_set_definitions_nested():\n    \"\"\"Recursion through nested Object/Array structures.\"